'''Alduin''', or the '''World-Eater''', as he is known to the residents of [[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]], is an immensely powerful [[Skyrim:Dragon|Dragon]], and the main antagonist of the [[SR:Main Quest|Main Quest]]. He is depicted as a malevolent force who destroys the world periodically, and the [[Skyrim:Nord|Nords]] believe that his reappearance heralds the end of time. He is the self-proclaimed First-Born of [[Lore:Akatosh|Akatosh]]. His name can be separated into "Al-Du-In", which means "Destroyer-Devour-Master" in Dragon Language.

He has a 50% resistance to fire and a 25% weakness to frost, and knows the [[Skyrim:Fire Breath|Fire Breath]], [[Skyrim:Frost Breath|Frost Breath]] and [[Skyrim:Unrelenting Force|Unrelenting Force]] shouts, as well as the [[Skyrim:Dragon Storm Call|Dragon Storm Call]] shout unique to him.
{{NewLeft}}

==Resurrection of Dragons==
During the quest [[Skyrim:A Blade in the Dark|A Blade in the Dark]], Alduin resurrects the dead dragon [[Skyrim:Sahloknir|Sahloknir]] from his burial place, revealing how the rest of the dragons have returned after being slain centuries ago. After this quest, you may get to see the rare occasion where Alduin resurrects another, leveled dragon.

When resurrecting other dragons, Alduin can be spotted from a distance, and more easily heard thanks to his roars. It's easy to distinguish Alduin from other dragons, as he will stay far in the distance, flying around, unlike normal wild dragons (who will fly right to you). Alduin won't leave this location until you approach {{vn|plain}}, and as soon as you get close enough, he will say "(dragon name) ''{{hover|Your soul is bound to me for eternity!|zil gro dovah ulse!}}''" then use the shout ''"{{hover| Flesh-Time-Undo|Slen Tiid Vo!}}"''. A new dragon will appear (having been resurrected) and respond to Alduin, after which Alduin flies away and the resurrected dragon attacks you. It is possible to interrupt the resurrection by attacking Alduin, which causes him to become hostile and fly away {{vn|plain}}.

Alduin will have a brief conversation during resurrection. He will say the name of either [[SR:Vuljotnaak|Vuljotnaak]], [[SR:Viinturuth|Viinturuth]], or [[SR:Nahagliiv|Nahagliiv]], depending on which dragon he is resurrecting:
:'''(dragon name):''' ''"{{hover|Alduin, my lord!|Alduin, thuri!}}"''
:'''Alduin:''' ''"{{hover|Arise|Alok}}, (dragon name). {{hover|(The) time has come.|Tiid boaan.}}"''

