==Quest-Related Events==
===Unbound===
Moments before you are to be executed in [[SR:Helgen|Helgen]], Alduin lands in the town and begins to unleash carnage, incidentally allowing you to escape execution with [[SR:Ralof|Ralof]]. His movement throughout the town will follow you as you progress. First, he will break open the watchtower containing Ralof and [[SR:Ulfric Stormcloak|Jarl Ulfric Stormcloak]], killing a [[SR:Stormcloak Soldier|Stormcloak Soldier]]. Next, he will kill [[SR:Torolf|Torolf]] with his Fire Breath shout near [[SR:Hadvar|Hadvar]]. Alduin will then land on a wall as you and Hadvar pass near it, before taking to the skies and moving freely throughout the town, Shouting at various soldiers.

While destroying the town, Alduin may speak in the [[Lore:Dragon Language|Dragon language]]:
:''"{{hover|Your soul will feed my hunger.|Hin sil fen nahkip bahloki.}}"''
:''"{{hover|Those who (do) not bow will be devoured.|Nust wo ni qiilaan fen kos duaan.}}"''

Throughout [[SR:Helgen Keep|Helgen Keep]], the battle with Alduin in the town rages on, causing door blockages and cave-ins within the dungeon. After at last escaping, Alduin can be seen soaring away, flying over [[SR:Bleak Falls Barrow (place)|Bleak Falls Barrow]] to an unknown location.

===A Blade in the Dark===
While resurrecting Sahloknir in Kynesgrove:
:'''Alduin:''' ''"{{hover|Sahloknir, your soul is bound to me for eternity!|Sahloknir, ziil gro dovah ulse!}} Slen Tiid Vo!"''

When the dragon, Sahloknir, is whole once more, he has a conversation in the dragon language with Alduin:
:'''Sahloknir:''' ''"{{hover|Alduin, my lord! (Is it) time (to) restore (the) ancient dominion?|Alduin, thuri! Boaan tiid vokriiha suleyksejun kruziik?}}"''
:'''Alduin:''' ''"{{hover|Yes, Sahloknir, my allied champion.|Geh, Sahloknir, kaali mir.}}

Turning to you:
''"{{hover|So, you are Dragonborn? I see no dragon in you.|Ful, losei Dovahkiin? Zu'u koraav nid nol dov do hi.}} You do not even know our tongue, do you? Such arrogance, to dare take for yourself the name of Dovah. {{hover|Sahloknir, kill this mortal.|Sahloknir, krii daar joorre.}}"''

After ordering Sahloknir to kill you, Alduin flies away.

===Alduin's Bane===
====Time Wound====
While the Nords draw their weapons, Alduin will land atop the word wall and speak: 

'''Alduin''': ''"{{hover|Fools!|Meyye!}} {{hover|Treacherous slaves!|Tahrodiis aanne!}} {{hover|Your hopes (are) all withered!|Him hinde pah liiv!}} {{hover|I (am) your doom!|Zu'u hin daan!}}"''<br>
'''Gormlaith''': ''"Let those that watch from Sovngarde envy us this day!"''

At this point, the Nords will release the [[Skyrim:Dragonrend|Dragonrend]] Shout. When they Shout, you will automatically learn it. In the skies, Alduin will feel mortality rise through his body and will be forced to land: 

'''Alduin''': ''"{{hover|Cowardly mortals!|Nivahriin joorre!}} What have you done? What twisted Words have you created?! {{hover|Treacherous|Tahrodiis}} Paarthurnax! My teeth to his neck! But first... {{hover|die in terror|dir ko maar}}. You will die in terror, knowing your final fate... To feed my power when I come for you in Sovngarde!"''<br>
'''Gormlaith''': ''"If I die today, it will not be in terror. You feel fear for the first time, worm. I see it in your eyes. Skyrim will be free!"''

The three Nords will then proceed to attack the World-Eater, but to no avail. Alduin will pick up Gormlaith between his teeth and fling her to the right, killing her: 

'''Hakon''': ''"No, damn you! It's no use! Use the Scroll, Felldir! Now!"''<br>
'''Felldir''': ''"Hold, Alduin on the Wing! [[Lore:Kyne|Sister Hawk]], grant us your sacred breath to make this contract heard! Begone, World-Eater! By words with older bones than your own we break your perch on this age and send you out! You are banished! Alduin, we shout you out from all our endings unto the last!"''<br>
'''Alduin''': ''"{{hover|The (Elder) Scroll...?! Cowards...|Faal Kel...?! Nikriinne...}}"''

A surprised Alduin will futilely breathe fire at Felldir before disappearing into the flow of time, to an unknown era.
====Present====
Directly after the cutscene, when you arrive back in the present, Alduin will appear at the Throat of the World, shouting: 
:'''Alduin:''' ''"{{hover|My hunger has been fed by mortal souls.|Bahloki nahkip sillesejoor.}} My belly is full of the souls of your fellow mortals, Dovahkiin. Die now and await your fate in Sovngarde!"''
:'''Paarthurnax:''' ''"{{hover|You fail.|Lost funt.}} You are too late, Alduin! Dovahkiin! Use Dragonrend, if you know it!"''
:'''Alduin:''' ''"{{hover|My power (is) strong|Suleyki mulaag}}, Paarthurnax. My power has waxed, while yours has waned. {{hover|Join or die.|Aav uv dir.}} Join me or perish with your mortal friends."''
:'''Paarthurnax:''' ''"{{hover|Ceaseless enemy!|Unslaad hokoron!}} Never again!"''

[[File:SR-quest-Alduin's Bane 02.jpg|thumb|Alduin battles Paarthurnax at the Throat of the World]]
Paarthurnax and Alduin will take flight, attacking each other in the air. During the battle, Alduin may say some of the following taunts: 
:''"Dovahkiin, you call yourself? Arrogant mortal."''
:''"{{hover|(I) will devour your souls in Sovngarde!|Fen du hin sille ko Sovngarde!}}"''
:''"I will feast on your soul in Sovngarde!"''
:''"You are no match for me, {{hover|mortal!|joor!}}"''
:''"Paarthurnax is weak. I am strong."''
:''"My time has come again."''
:''"{{hover|Terror awaits in Sovngarde|Maar saraan ko Sovngarde.}}"''
:''"I have feasted on many greater than you."''
:''"You will pay for your defiance!"''
:''"You may have picked up the weapons of my ancient foes, but you are not their equal!"''

When Alduin is grounded he may say:
:''"My teeth to your neck, Dovahkiin!"''

When Alduin's health drops to zero, he says: 
:''"{{hover|You've become strong, Dragonborn.|Meyz mul, Dovahkiin.}} You have become strong. But I am {{hover|Destroyer-Devour-Master|Al-du-in}}, Firstborn of Akatosh! {{hover|My strength is the greatest!|Mulaagi zok lot!}} I cannot be slain here, by you or anyone else! You cannot prevail against me. I will outlast you... mortal!"'' 

He will then fly off to [[SR:Skuldafn|Skuldafn]] to regain his power.

===Dragonslayer===
After traveling to [[SR:Sovngarde (place)|Sovngarde]] and discovering Alduin's Soul Snare, the player will have to navigate through the fog in search of the [[SR:Hall of Valor|Hall of Valor]]. Alduin appears at multiple points within the mist, either lurking on ground-level or soaring overhead. If you take too long, Alduin will swoop down and kill a Stormcloak Soldier and an [[SR:Imperial Soldier|Imperial Soldier]].

Returning to the outdoors of Sovngarde from the Hall of Valor with the three ancient Nord heroes will launch an attempt to dispel Alduin's Soul Snare. After using [[SR:Clear Skies|Clear Skies]]:
:'''Alduin:''' ''"Ven Mul Riik!"''
:'''Gormlaith:''' ''"Again!"''
:'''Felldir:''' ''"We can shatter his power if we Shout together!"''

After Shouting again:
:'''Alduin:''' ''"Ven Mul Riik!"''
:'''Hakon:''' ''"Does his strength have no end? Is our struggle in vain?"''
:'''Gormlaith:''' ''"Stand fast! His strength is failing! Once more, and his might will be broken!"''
:'''Felldir:''' ''"His power crumbles - do not pause for breath!"''

As he flies in:
:'''Alduin:''' ''"Face me, then! {{hover|I am Alduin!|Zu'u Alduin!}}"''

With his fog shield dissipated, Alduin will have no choice but to face you in open combat. He is immune to damage until hit by Dragonrend. Alduin is functionally very similar to most other dragons, his only significant difference being a tendency to crawl backwards while Shouting, creating distance between him and his attacker. With the three Nord heroes on your side (and potentially [[SR:Tsun|Tsun]], if Alduin attacks him), Alduin should go down fairly easily. Avoid his fire breath, as it can be deadly even for high level players. If you are having trouble defeating him, range counters him fairly well.

During the battle, Alduin may use the following taunts, issued to either you or the Nord heroes:
:''"You are persistent, Dovahkiin. {{hover|Good as (a) slave.|Pruzah ol aar.}} A fine slave you would have made."''
:''"{{hover|Dragonborn, your pride will be humbled.|Dovahkiin, hin kah fen kos bonaar.}}"''[[File:SR-quest-Dragonslayer 02.jpg|thumb|The death of Alduin]]
:''"{{hover|I have returned.|Zu'u lost daal.}}"''
:''"I have already defeated your friends once. {{hover|Scorn.|Beyn.}} I do not fear them."''
:''"{{hover|The Elder Scroll did not defeat me.|Kel drey ni viik.}}"''
:''"{{hover|My children will rise.|Di kiirre fen alok.}}"''
:''"{{hover|This world is mine.|Daar Lein los dii.}}"''
:''"{{hover|Arrogant mortals! Your pride will be humbled.|Pahlok joorre! Hin kah fen kos bonaar.}}"''
:''"{{hover|I (am still) Alduin, most mighty of any in Mundus (the world).|Zu'u Alduin, zok sahrot do naan ko Lein.}}"''
:''"{{hover|I've killed you once, now your souls will feed my power.|Zu'u lost kriaan hi ont, nu hin sille fen nahkip suleyki.}}"''
:''"{{hover|Dragonborn|Dovahkiin}}, you should not have come here. {{hover|Now your soul (is) mine.|Nu hin sil dii.}}"''
:''"{{hover|I do not fear mortal ghosts.|Zu'u ni faas gaaffesejul.}}"''


When Alduin's health is fully depleted, he will enter a hunched state and become immune to all damage, other than the player. Be sure to heal if you are on low health, as the meteors can still kill you and Alduin will never recover. After dealing the final blow, Alduin will writhe and thrash, screaming:
:'''Alduin:''' ''"{{hover|I am unending! I cannot end!|Zu'u unslaad! Zu'u nis oblaan!}}

After crying out, Alduin explodes, leaving behind a wispy, golden-glowing black skeleton which soon fades away. With Alduin dead, Sovngarde returns to its ethereal state and the main story of Skyrim comes to an end.

==Notes==
* Alduin has a special passive ability, "AbAlduinInvulnerability" in the editor, which renders him invulnerable to harm so long as he is not affected by Dragonrend (or, as the conditions on the effect detail, "is allowed to fly").
* If you encounter Alduin during the resurrection of a dragon, he can be hit with any long-ranged attack. However, it appears that he is not actually hit, as no health bar appears. He does appear as hostile at that moment, showing as a red dot on your compass. The red dot will disappear after Alduin flies away again.
* During the resurrection of a dragon, Alduin will occasionally Shout, darkening the sky.
* Alduin has a unique Shout called Dragon Storm Call, which is very similar to [[Skyrim:Storm Call|Storm Call]], and causes fiery meteors to rain from the sky.
* If you deal enough damage to him when he is resurrecting a dragon, he will crash land on the ground, then take flight again and fly off.
* Alduin is voiced by [[wikipedia:Daniel Riordan|Daniel Riordan]].
* [[General:Adam Adamowicz|Adam Adamowicz]] and [[General:Jonah Lobe|Jonah Lobe]] designed [[Lore:Alduin|Alduin]] by using the texture of meteorites as a basis.
* There's a very small chance that Alduin will use Unrelenting Force on you if you try to damage him while he is resurrecting a dragon.
* The version of Alduin encountered in the past during [[Skyrim:Alduin's Bane|Alduin's Bane]] (BaseID <code>4377F</code>, RefID <code>4377E</code>), is a static level 100 and boasts 6905 health.
*If the [[Skyrim:Dawnguard|Dawnguard]] add-on is installed and you defeat Alduin before starting [[Skyrim:Beyond Death|Beyond Death]], [[Skyrim:Durnehviir (dragon)|Durnehviir]] will be impressed and say ''"Even in the Soul Cairn, the defeat of the World Eater has reached my ears, Dovahkiin. You may not be dovah, but the defeat of Alduin earns you the right of title."''
*If the [[Skyrim:Dragonborn|Dragonborn]] add-on is installed and you defeat Alduin before starting [[Skyrim:At the Summit of Apocrypha|At the Summit of Apocrypha]], [[Skyrim:Miraak (person)|Miraak]] will be impressed and say ''"Felling Alduin was a mighty deed, and I thank you for it. He would have proved troublesome to me."''
*It is impossible to loot Alduin, even though the option presents itself while his body dissipates. However, it is possible to harvest [[Skyrim:Dragon Heartscales|dragon heartscales]] from him.
*Alduin's soul is not absorbed. You can later discuss the ramifications of this with [[Skyrim:Arngeir|Arngeir]] unless you have antagonized him by killing [[Skyrim:Paarthurnax_(dragon)|Paarthurnax]].
*Alduin is the highest level dragon in the game; boasting a max level of 100. 
*Alduin's damage scales as the player levels up; at level 100 his breath is equivalent to an ancient dragon. Interestingly, his bite damage remains static, always being that of a regular dragon.
*Alduin is the only dragon in the game that can use both fire and frost breath.

== Bugs ==
{{Bug|When encountering Alduin raising a dragon as a random encounter, chasing him off before he completes the resurrection causes the dragon burial mound to become stuck in the 'bonfire of energy' state.|confirmed=1}} 
**{{Pc22}} This can be fixed using the console, at least as far as the visual effects go: look upwards at the 'bonfire', open the console, click on the fire effect and use the ''disable'' command. Look at the middle of the dragon mound, click on it, and use the ''disable'' command again. This will make both the special effect and the mound cover disappear.
{{Bug|After learning [[Skyrim:Dragonrend|Dragonrend]] during [[Skyrim:Alduin's Bane|Alduin's Bane]], Alduin will sometimes be invincible.|OSP|1.9}}
**Escaping the battle by running down the Throat of the World and fast-traveling back appears to make him vulnerable to damage again.
{{Bug|Alduin's death cry during [[Skyrim:Dragonslayer|Dragonslayer]] may be too quiet for you to hear if you're too far away.|USKP|1.2.2}}

